//! The LP2985, Texas Instruments, 150 mA low-noise low-dropout regulator with shutdown, fixed
//! 3.3 V, in the 5-pin SOT-23 package (DBV): the U2 of the Power Manifold charger module (LCSC
//! C89826, which is the LP2985A-33DBVR, the 1 % grade; `catalogs/lp2985.csv`).
//!
//! The standard `LinearRegulator` has a pin table for three pins only (and none for the
//! 5-pin SOT-23), so the part provides it with its own: TI's "LP2985 150-mA Low-noise
//! Low-dropout Regulator With Shutdown", SLVS522O (July 2004, revised January 2015), section 5
//! (printed page 3), DBV (SOT-23) package: pin 1 `VIN`, 2 `GND`, 3 `ON/OFF`, 4 `BYPASS`, 5 `VOUT`.
//! `ON/OFF` is an active-low shutdown input that the datasheet says to tie to VIN if unused
//! (and not to leave open: section 7.4.2, "do not leave ON/OFF unconnected", and section 8.1.2,
//! "ON/OFF must be actively terminated"), so it is an
//! `input` that must be connected. `BYPASS` takes the 10 nF capacitor that lowers the noise
//! (section 5, Pin Functions: "Attach a 10-nF capacitor to improve low-noise performance"; section 8.1.2: "Optional BYPASS capacitor"), and the part works
//! without one: it is `passive`, and a passive pin may float.
//!
//! What is deliberately left out: the ON/OFF thresholds (1.4 V high at 25 C and 1.6 V over
//! temperature, 0.55 V low at 25 C and 0.15 V over temperature, Table 6.5) as logic levels, the
//! capacitor and ESR requirements of the output, and the power rating (see the row's notes).

import std::parts::regulator::LinearRegulator

/// The LP2985A-33: 3.3 V, 150 mA, in SOT-23-5.
part Lp2985 provides LinearRegulator {
    pins "SOT-23-5" {
        //  pin       kind     name      pads
        .vin.pos  power   "VIN"     "1"
        .vin.neg  power   "GND"     "2"
        .on_off   input   "ON/OFF"  "3"
        .bypass   passive "BYPASS"  "4"
        .vout.pos power   "VOUT"    "5"
    }

    // Table 6.5 (printed page 5), IL = 0, VON/OFF = 2 V: the GND pin current, 125 uA at most over
    // -40 C to 125 C (95 uA at 25 C), with the output unloaded.
    .quiescent_current &= 0A..125uA

    catalog lp2985 by .mpn { .mpn, .package, .vout.voltage, .dropout, .max_current }
}
